WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-26, with W26 (interactive startup)


STATE

  Version 0.3.7 loads an optional XDG rc before the first interactive
  prompt. --norc skips it. The guidance builtin prints the same key
  help as the Ctrl+G overlay. Normal and sanitizer suites pass.

  Phase P4 complete (arrays, [[ ]]/=~, local/declare,
  brace expansion, process substitution, ** globstar, strict modes,
  abbreviations, man-page completion generator, and -v / --version), on
  branch dev. 0.3.5 adds -v as a CLI synonym for --version.
  0.3.4 adds:
  - fish-style interactive abbreviations in include/tam-clam/abbr.h,
    src/abbr.c, src/edit/edit.c, src/edit/highlight.c, src/builtins.c,
    and src/shell.c: `abbr` builtin (-a/-e/-q/-l/-s, -p command|anywhere,
    NAME=EXPANSION shorthand), in-place expansion on Space and Enter
    outside quotes (undoable with Ctrl+Z so history records the real
    command), and valid-command syntax highlighting;
  - man-page completion generator tools/tam-clam-gen-comp (POSIX sh +
    awk, installed to $(BINDIR)/tam-clam-gen-comp by `make install`)
    writing .comp files directly into tam-clam's XDG completion path;
  - tests/test_abbr.c (39 checks covering abbr table/builtin, line
    editor expansion/undo/quoting, and end-to-end tam-clam-gen-comp ->
    tc_complete loading) and sandbox/demo-0.3.4-abbr-compgen.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test, make sanitize, and make
  fuzz pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tam-idol/keys/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  keys/keybindings.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default; ** recursive globbing is off by default;
  strict modes are opt-in and off by default.


